', start=''):\n542 |     \"\"\"\n543 |     Simple matching of version numbers, for use in CCompiler and FCompiler.\n544 | \n545 |     Parameters\n546 |     ----------\n547 |     pat : str, optional\n548 |         A regular expression matching version numbers.\n549 |         Default is ``r'[-.\\\\d]+'``.\n550 |     ignore : str, optional\n551 |         A regular expression matching patterns to skip.\n552 |         Default is ``''``, in which case nothing is skipped.\n553 |     start : str, optional\n554 |         A regular expression matching the start of where to start looking\n555 |         for version numbers.\n556 |         Default is ``''``, in which case searching is started at the\n557 |         beginning of the version string given to `matcher`.\n558 | \n559 |     Returns\n560 |     -------\n561 |     matcher : callable\n562 |         A function that is appropriate to use as the ``.version_match``\n563 |         attribute of a `CCompiler` class. `matcher` takes a single parameter,\n564 |         a version string.\n565 | \n566 |     \"\"\"\n567 |     def matcher(self, version_string):\n568 |         # version string may appear in the second line, so getting rid\n569 |         # of new lines:\n570 |         version_string = version_string.replace('\\n', ' ')\n571 |         pos = 0\n572 |         if start:\n573 |             m = re.match(start, version_string)\n574 |             if not m:\n575 |                 return None\n576 |             pos = m.end()\n577 |         while True:\n578 |             m = re.search(pat, version_string[pos:])\n579 |             if not m:\n580 |                 return None\n581 |             if ignore and re.match(ignore, m.group(0)):\n582 |                 pos = m.end()\n583 |                 continue\n584 |             break\n585 |         return m.group(0)\n586 |     return matcher\n```\n\nFound function `numpy/distutils/command/build_src.py:build_src.filter_py_files`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\