`\n1918 | def _generate_get_feature_names_out(estimator, n_features_out, input_features=None):\n1919 |     \"\"\"Generate feature names out for estimator using the estimator name as the prefix.\n1920 | \n1921 |     The input_feature names are validated but not used. This function is useful\n1922 |     for estimators that generate their own names based on `n_features_out`, i.e. PCA.\n1923 | \n1924 |     Parameters\n1925 |     ----------\n1926 |     estimator : estimator instance\n1927 |         Estimator producing output feature names.\n1928 | \n1929 |     n_feature_out : int\n1930 |         Number of feature names out.\n1931 | \n1932 |     input_features : array-like of str or None, default=None\n1933 |         Only used to validate feature names with `estimator.feature_names_in_`.\n1934 | \n1935 |     Returns\n1936 |     -------\n1937 |     feature_names_in : ndarray of str or `None`\n1938 |         Feature names in.\n1939 |     \"\"\"\n1940 |     _check_feature_names_in(estimator, input_features, generate_names=False)\n1941 |     estimator_name = estimator.__class__.__name__.lower()\n1942 |     return np.asarray(\n1943 |         [f\"{estimator_name}{i}\" for i in range(n_features_out)], dtype=object\n1944 |     )\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSRegression.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n634 | def fit(self, X, Y):\n635 |         \"\"\"Fit model to data.\n636 | \n637 |         Parameters\n638 |         ----------\n639 |         X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n640 |             Training vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n641 |             `n_features` is the number of predictors.\n642 | \n643 |         Y : array-like of shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_targets)\n644 |             Target vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n645 |             `n_targets` is the number of response variables.\n646 | \n647 |         Returns\n648 |         -