ed_indices = np.empty(shape=total_nnz, dtype=index_dtype)\n77 |     expanded_indptr = np.empty(shape=X.indptr.shape[0], dtype=index_dtype)\n78 |     _csr_polynomial_expansion(\n79 |         X.data,\n80 |         X.indices,\n81 |         X.indptr,\n82 |         X.shape[1],\n83 |         expanded_data,\n84 |         expanded_indices,\n85 |         expanded_indptr,\n86 |         interaction_only,\n87 |         deg,\n88 |     )\n89 |     return sparse.csr_matrix(\n90 |         (expanded_data, expanded_indices, expanded_indptr),\n91 |         shape=(X.indptr.shape[0] - 1, expanded_col),\n92 |         dtype=X.dtype,\n93 |     )\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/metrics/pairwise.py:polynomial_kernel`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1277 | def polynomial_kernel(X, Y=None, degree=3, gamma=None, coef0=1):\n1278 |     \"\"\"\n1279 |     Compute the polynomial kernel between X and Y.\n1280 | \n1281 |         K(X, Y) = (gamma <X, Y> + coef0) ^ degree\n1282 | \n1283 |     Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <polynomial_kernel>`.\n1284 | \n1285 |     Parameters\n1286 |     ----------\n1287 |     X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples_X, n_features)\n1288 |         A feature array.\n1289 | \n1290 |     Y : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples_Y, n_features), default=None\n1291 |         An optional second feature array. If `None`, uses `Y=X`.\n1292 | \n1293 |     degree : float, default=3\n1294 |         Kernel degree.\n1295 | \n1296 |     gamma : float, default=None\n1297 |         Coefficient of the vector inner product. If None, defaults to 1.0 / n_features.\n1298 | \n1299 |     coef0 : float, default=1\n1300 |         Constant offset added to scaled inner product.\n1301 | \n1302 |     Returns\n1303 |     -------\n1304 |     Gram matrix : ndarray of shape (n_samples_X, n_samples_Y)\n1305 |         The polynomial kernel.\n1306 |     \"\"\"\n1307 |     X, Y = check_pairwise_arrays(X, Y)\n1308 |     if gamma is None:\n1309 |        